+# Owner-authorized Work Harness phase autonomy implementation
+
+The owner's current instruction authorizes changing the workflow before research
+resumes. No further approval is needed. Research is paused; original evidence,
+unknown-run identities, budgets and optional-scope authority must be preserved.
+
+Implement explicit phase_autonomy with bundled milestone evidence, real native
+calls inside the claimed command worker, scoped one-child dispatch, one independent
+phase review and preserved B05/M05/E gates. Add C core-paper/code/strong-method
+basis as a required finding, and checked discussion leads. Preserve legacy mode.
+
+Validate on the authorized hn01 GPU host: aggregation/scope/freeze, real parent and
+native subprocess/receipt, fencing, idempotency, unfinished-child completion,
+phase coverage chain, D-to-E lineage, revisits and existing runtime behavior.
+Independent review precedes installation. Export .8, install through local
+marketplace for main/private profiles, adopt at quiet paused revision with backup,
+then resume one existing guarded consumer. Publish source patch and factual logs
+to the existing SPECTRUM research branch. Report scientific results separately
+from software checks; no scientific experiment is completed by this maintenance.
