+# Phase autonomy .8 source review and verification
+
+Owner request: sustained phase worker with internal mathematics/code/GPU/debug
+iteration; C grounded in core-paper implementation, strong methods and checked
+community leads. Research stayed paused at revision247 during this maintenance.
+
+Independent static reviewers: cd_integration_map and cd_final_review. They found
+and the implementation repaired D-to-E aggregate lineage, interior-phase rewind,
+mandatory C.method_basis, qualification/pending-scoring checks, cross-attempt
+coverage retention, request idempotency and cycle-closure native registration.
+Final production-code review reported no remaining important issue. Reviews are
+software assessments, not independent scientific experiment acceptance.
+
+All executable checks ran on authorized hn01 host, using its existing Python
+3.12 venv. No Mac experiment or code test was run.
+- 35 new phase tests: aggregation, real native subprocess/receipts, single child,
+  parent fencing and unresolved-work completion, cross-worker checkpoint,
+  actual shared phase acceptance/audit, D-to-E freeze and revisits.
+- 49 phase plus legacy admission checks passed (overlaps full suite).
+- 451 runtime checks passed in 198.980 seconds.
+- 34 plugin checks passed; node check errors=[] (source navigation only).
+
+The initial broad run had seven legacy admission fixture failures. The untouched
+.7 source reproduced all seven. The legacy method-batch fixture now explicitly
+uses a copied non-Harness Skill, as its protocol requires. Real Harness/CD tests
+retain the marker and mandatory decision admission. No production checks were
+relaxed. Initial and parent comparison logs are retained alongside final logs.
+
+These are software checks with synthetic fixtures; they report no new SPECTRUM
+scientific result. Installation, live adoption and resume have separate receipts.
