@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Sustained phase execution and research iteration
+
+Select `sequence.execution_mode: phase_autonomy` together with
+`flow_profile: work-harness-cd-v1` for new Work Harness programs. This explicit
+mode overrides inherited one-agent-per-node and propose-every-edit instructions.
+Older pinned programs retain their behavior until a quiet, recorded adoption.
+
+## One sustained worker per meaningful phase
+
+A worker covers the remaining consecutive milestones of a phase, autonomously
+reading sources, deriving mathematics, designing experiments, editing code,
+executing on the fixed GPU and debugging from actual results. Milestones retain
+all evidence obligations; they do not each start a new worker/reviewer round.
+C from S01 (or the current B02) through B05 is one assignment. D H01 through M05
+is one assignment. E design through G02 protocol freeze is a boundary, followed
+by E execution through G05. Literature, analysis, authorized writing and other
+scopes are likewise grouped. Initial B01 official setup remains a setup boundary;
+excluded optional scopes never become authorized through aggregation.
+
+The worker can revisit papers, code, Xiaohongshu discussion leads and earlier
+local hypotheses at any time. No special handoff is needed for ordinary B/C/D
+thinking and experiments inside an unaccepted phase. A substantive revision of
+an already accepted problem/method uses the typed revisit route; if its target
+is inside a jointly accepted phase, the program reopens that whole phase and
+its dependent suffix while preserving the requested target and all old evidence.
+
+One separate reviewer accepts the complete phase evidence. B05 still requires a
+supported condition/failure/dependency and actual native scoring; M05 still
+requires VERIFIED_FOR_SCALEUP and scorer replay. Accepted D automatically enters
+E. Formal E comparison fairness, freeze, scale, uncertainty and confirmation are
+not replaced by small development experiments.
+
+## C starts from real methods and implementations
+
+`C.method_basis` is a mandatory worker AND reviewer requirement. Identify the
+nearest core papers and their actual official code revisions, entry points,
+inherited settings and task-relevant strong alternatives. Bind the selected
+model/data/benchmark/native evaluation. Record selection and exclusion reasons,
+implementation or reproduction gaps, and verify any current-SOTA claim against
+primary evidence for the same task. Existing project self-training controls alone
+cannot qualify as this basis.
+
+Use the user's existing Xiaohongshu read-only choice. Read discussion/troubleshooting
+posts and implementation experiences, then trace claims to primary sources and
+code before testing. Retain unavailable access explicitly and continue independent
+research; a post is not scientific evidence or permission to contact its author.
+
+C makes a mathematical condition or suspected unnecessary dependency measurable
+using existing methods, models and datasets. D develops a mechanism and implements
+its predicted intervention, comparing it with qualified strong/simple controls.
+Follow the evidence through repeated B/C/D work. Do not freeze an old convenient
+F/P/A-style plan before examining the closest published implementation.
+
+## Real GPU execution inside the worker
+
+The CommandWorker injects `response_protocol.phase_native` only after a real
+controller claim. Its context binds project/run/owner/fence to the current live
+phase worker. Invoke the supplied `phase-native --context ... --request ...`
+command with one request containing `request_id`, `task`, `decision_ref`, and
+`coverage_ref`. The task is native_harness/native, never another general agent.
+Synchronize pinned input/code files to the already fixed target; the existing
+NativeBridge verifies pins and performs actual execution and output collection.
+Do not fabricate future run IDs or receipts to satisfy an input schema.
+
+The request passes canonical scientific admission, fixed-target and source checks,
+B01 scope where applicable, stage predecessors, native protocol and coverage checks.
+There is no separate model review per preparation/train/debug call. The child has
+its own actual run, logs, outputs and receipt. Only one native child may be live;
+unknown jobs retain that slot and must be reconciled under their original identity.
+A repeated identical request observes the same child; changed content with the
+same request ID is rejected. The parent cannot complete with unresolved children.
+
+Every subsequent request extends the latest worker-local decision and coverage;
+the final phase result extends them again and consumes all actual native receipts,
+including failures. Pending scoring and formal E obligations cannot disappear.
+Local selection is not scientific acceptance. Return `tasks: []` with all phase
+findings; code prohibits the old chain of tiny source/design/code agent tasks.
+
+The worker may retain checkpoints across transport interruptions; interruption does
+not finish the phase or reset budget. No new aggregate round cap is imposed.
+Existing project authority still applies: child compute plus collection must fit
+the remaining invocation; parent wall time and native time are conservatively
+counted separately. Scientific workloads and code tests use the authorized GPU
+host. The Mac hosts orchestration only; no Docker or new local model is introduced.
